{"at":"2026-10-30T00:07:25.937Z","component":"OpenPGP signature transport selection","evidence":["01bfd3581d9e8674299a4bd436d41cdcf6cb8d67f35b8eb84b15b26408adf620","18e3d0b244f53abe8455069907ce6a66dfcdddd47c9c7ed61cf034f501fdcade","56dde532749cc7f942bbcfeb7047dced278dd25d795d651dd1814c8ff4fa8c85","7089a7208bb7a5695b4ba53aded977dde7f7184ce9faa36daf208d3af041bbc6","cdf3234a2244b38cac1ca27e714645c6722f8b6a49ad82fdd78d0909e833f270","f77688b3bb7c8ce54a08a37b00ea07d6259f7452f9a762049b015c43d5cf5c26"],"id":"258b90d7e4be92fc0ae99e668514f105cb24994627f55d74a41684cfbdc2270c","kind":"lesson","paths":["mail/extensions/am-e2e/prefs/e2e-prefs.js","mail/extensions/openpgp/content/modules/constants.sys.mjs","mail/extensions/openpgp/content/ui/enigmailMsgComposeOverlay.js","mailnews/compose/public/nsIMsgComposeSecure.idl"],"quotes":[{"id":"cdf3234a2244b38cac1ca27e714645c6722f8b6a49ad82fdd78d0909e833f270","text":"pref(\"mail.openpgp.clear_signature_format\", \"multipart\");"},{"id":"f77688b3bb7c8ce54a08a37b00ea07d6259f7452f9a762049b015c43d5cf5c26","text":"SEND_SIG_UNOBTRUSIVE: 0x10000,"},{"id":"56dde532749cc7f942bbcfeb7047dced278dd25d795d651dd1814c8ff4fa8c85","text":"if (sendFlags & SIGN && !(sendFlags & ENCRYPT)) {"},{"id":"01bfd3581d9e8674299a4bd436d41cdcf6cb8d67f35b8eb84b15b26408adf620","text":"attribute AUTF8String signFormat;"}],"repository":"thunderbird","source":{"basis":"Quoted evidence supports the claim; its interpretation still needs current-source checks.","revision":"0b93f0f7a926ed94c8a0646f18b6734ec7cc0f6d","sourceAt":"2026-10-05T22:44:59Z","type":"extraction"},"status":"supported","supersedes":[],"text":"The clear_signature_format default is multipart. Compose adds SEND_SIG_UNOBTRUSIVE only inside its PGP/MIME signed-only branch when the preference equals unobtrusive. It also exposes the selected transport through the shared signFormat string property consumed during MIME construction. The S/MIME class's accessors satisfy that shared interface; they do not by themselves implement this OpenPGP transport. Encrypted output keeps its separate mode path.","title":"Unobtrusive signature generation is an opt-in signed-only MIME mode","version":1,"visibility":"shared"}
